<title>FINLAND: Finnair Feb load factor up at 67.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Finnair Feb load factor up at 67.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish national airline Finnair Oy said in a statement on Friday its passenger load factor rose 2.6 percentage points year-on-year in February to 67.7 percent.  </p>
<p>Finnair gave the following statistics:</p>
<p>					Feb 1997    Jan 1997   Yr/yr(pct)</p>
<p> Passengers (thousand)	     474	   478	  +3.1</p>
<p> RPK (million)			 866	   917	  +2.8</p>
<p> RTK (million)			 100	   105	  +6.6</p>
<p> Cargo and mail (thousand kg)  5,568	 5,554	 +13.6</p>
<p> Passenger load factor (pct)    67.7	  66.3	  +2.6 pts</p>
<p>@</p>
<p>February 1997 totals broken down by flight type:</p>
<p>			Passengers   RPK	 RTK	    Cargo</p>
<p>			thousand   million    million     thousand kg</p>
<p> International	 244	 630	  78	    4,932</p>
<p> Domestic		194	  90	   8		506</p>
<p> Charter		  35	 146	  14		130</p>
<p>Load factor (percent) by flight type:</p>
<p>				  Feb 1997   Jan 1997   Yr/yr (pct pts)</p>
<p> International		  66.5	 65.5	  +3.0</p>
<p> Domestic			 54.3	 50.0	  +1.0</p>
<p>Finnair's financial year runs from April 1 to March 31. @</p>
<p>RPK - revenue passenger km (revenue passengers carried multiplied by km flown)</p>
<p>RTK - revenue tonne km (tonnage of revenue load carried -- passengers, cargo and mail -- multiplied by km flown.</p>
<p>Passenger load factor - RPK as a percentage of available seat km</p>
<p>Finnair does not give a cargo load factor. --Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
